// Move data, keyed by move NAME (not id) — every move's full data lives
// here exactly once, referenced by name from data/movesets.js.
//
// "Tackle": { type: "Normal", category: "Physical", power: 40, accuracy: 100,
//   pp: 35, description: "A physical attack in which the user charges and
//   slams into the target with its whole body." }
//
// Covers every move that exists through the end of Generation III (Ruby/
// Sapphire/Emerald) — 354 moves total, matching src/data/pokemon.js's
// Kanto/Johto/Hoenn coverage. Stats are CURRENT (Gen 9-era) values, not
// frozen Gen 3 numbers — some moves have had power/accuracy/PP rebalanced
// or even retyped (e.g. Charm, Moonlight, Sweet Kiss: Normal -> Fairy in
// Gen 6) since their original games. Source: pokemondb.net/move/generation/{1,2,3}.
// Moves introduced in Gen 4+ are a later pass, once more regions are added.
//
// Move-mechanics fields (0.2.5, TODO.md #10), appended after `description` on
// every entry and sourced from the PokeAPI clone — DATA ONLY, nothing on the
// detail screen reads any of them yet:
//   priority      moves.csv priority; 0 for most, negative for e.g. Roar.
//                 Always written, since 0 is a real value.
//   target        move_targets.csv identifier, stored as its raw hyphenated
//                 slug ("user", "selected-pokemon", "all-opponents"), the same
//                 convention evolutions.js uses for item/type slugs.
//   effectChance  moves.csv effect_chance — the secondary effect's odds.
//                 Omitted when blank.
//   flags         move_flags.csv identifiers via move_flag_map.csv
//                 ("contact", "protect", "sound", ...). Omitted when empty.
//   meta          move_meta.csv, as a sub-object so its `category`
//                 (move_meta_categories, e.g. "damage-ailment") can't collide
//                 with the top-level damage-class `category` above. Optional
//                 members: ailment, minHits/maxHits, minTurns/maxTurns, drain,
//                 healing, critRate, ailmentChance, flinchChance, statChance —
//                 each omitted at its own no-op value (blank, "none", or 0).
//                 The whole `meta` key is omitted when a move has no
//                 move_meta.csv row at all.
//   names         the same other-language set data/names.js stores per
//                 species, from move_names.csv. A language with no row is
//                 omitted — move_names.csv has NO roomaji rows at all, so no
//                 move ever carries `jaRomaji`. Separate from the detail
//                 screen's species-name popup, which reads names.js only.

